-- title:
--   Vertical unit in Jⁿ adapted to an end of the blown-up chart
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q \ge 5$, $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $\ell$ a prime with $\ell \ge 3$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$. Further data: a field $L$ of characteristic zero; an element $\xi \in L$ that is a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity; the hypothesis `hι` that there is a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota\xi = \exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$; an intermediate field $K$ of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ which by `hK` equals [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M'))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of [`CohCarrier.GammaH ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M')`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133), the level subgroup attached to the group of units of $\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell)^2M'$ congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$ (the kernel of reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell)^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times$).
--
--   The base ring is a discrete valuation ring $A$ which is a domain with fraction field $L$, henselian local, with algebraically closed residue field, and satisfies `hAq`: $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$, and `hξA`: $\xi$ lies in the image of $A$ in $L$; $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. An element $j \in K$ is given whose Laurent expansion is the coefficientwise image [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the $q$-expansion of the modular $j$-function, and $j \ne 0$. Finally $\varpi \in A$ generates $\mathfrak{m}_A$, and $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfies `hϖt`: $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   Write $C$ for `chartAlgFin A ↥K j`, the $A$-subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$. A maximal ideal $y$ of $C$ is given with `hϖy`: $\varpi \in y$, together with the supersingularity hypothesis `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of those $j$-invariants for which every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with that invariant has no nonzero $q$-torsion point.
--
--   The hypothesis `hArig` is a rigidity statement about the two-chart integral model $X =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) (the pushout gluing $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the $j$-chart and the $j^{-1}$-chart): for every point $z$ of $X$ at which the germ $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ (pulled back along `toBase`) lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and every point $y'$ of $\mathrm{Spec}\,C$ with `ιFin`$(y') = z$ at which the supersingularity condition for $j$ holds, there exist a complete discrete valuation ring $W$ which is a domain, a homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with $\mathfrak{m}_W = (\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f - (X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1) \in (X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of the stalk at $z$ onto $S = W[[X_0,X_1]]/(\sigma(\varpi_t^{q+1})v - fu)$, subject to seven further clauses (summarised here): $e$ sends the germ of each $a \in A$ to the constant $\sigma a$; every level automorphism attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ preserves $C$; those attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M') \cap \Gamma(\ell)$ act trivially modulo $y'$; each level automorphism acting trivially modulo $y'$ is linearised by some ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, a scalar $c \in W$ and a matrix $M$ over $W$ with $\theta$ fixing constants, $\theta(X_j) \equiv \sum_i M_{ij}X_i$ modulo the square of $(X_0,X_1)$, $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$, $M_{ij} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$, $c \equiv 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(\ell)$, and $c \not\equiv 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity; primes of $S$ containing $\sigma\varpi$ but not both $X_0,X_1$, whose linear parts $a_iX_0+b_iX_1$ satisfy $q \nmid a_1b_2-a_2b_1$, contract to distinct primes of the stalk; for the prime with linear part $X_0$, membership of the germ of $a \in C$ in its contraction is equivalent to all Laurent coefficients of $a$ lying in the image of $\mathfrak{m}_A$; and [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $C$ and, after subtraction of a suitable $a_0 \in A$ congruent to it modulo $y'$, corresponds under $e$ to a series $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ with $e_0 \ge 1$ whose degree-$e_0$ form $\sum_i h_{i,e_0-i}a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit for all $a,b \in W$ not both in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ with $a^qb-ab^q \in \mathfrak{m}_W$.
--
--   A particular such configuration is then fixed: a point $z$ of $X$, the germ $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ with `hz`: $\varpi_z \in \mathfrak{m}$ of the stalk, a point $y'$ of $\mathrm{Spec}\,C$ with `ιFin`$(y') = z$ and `hss'` its supersingularity, and `hy'y`: $y'$ corresponds to the ideal $y$; a ring $W_1$ (a complete discrete valuation ring and domain), a homomorphism $\sigma_1 : A \to W_1$ with $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1} = (\sigma_1\varpi)$, series $f_1,u_1,v_1$ with $u_1,v_1$ units and $f_1 \equiv X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and an isomorphism $e_1$ from the adic completion of the stalk at $z$ onto $S = W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{q+1})v_1 - f_1u_1)$. The hypothesis `hW₁` asserts for this data exactly the seven clauses listed above.
--
--   The remaining data are as follows. The ideal $J$ of $C$ is given by `hJ` as the infimum of the ideals obtained, for $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ a level automorphism of $K$ attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$, by pulling back the ideal generated by the images of $\sigma_1\varpi_t$, $X_0$ and $X_1$ in $S$ along $e_1 \circ (\text{completion}) \circ (\text{germ at } z)$ and then along the restriction of $\tau$ to $C$. The $A$-subalgebra $B$ of $K$ is, by `hB`, generated over $C$ by $\{x \in K : x\varpi_t \in J\}$, the $\varpi_t$-chart of the blow-up of the centre $J$. A valuation subring $W$ of $K$ contains $B$ (`hBW`). The hypothesis `hR1` has two clauses: $C \subseteq B$, and every element of $K$ is a quotient of elements of $B$ with nonzero denominator. The hypothesis `hR2` has three clauses: $A \to B$ is formally smooth, $A \to B$ is of finite presentation, and $B/(\varpi)$ has Krull dimension at most $1$. The hypothesis `hR3` has five clauses: an element of $L$ lies in $W$ exactly when it comes from $A$; $\mathfrak{m}_W$ is generated by $\varpi$; $W$ is a discrete valuation ring; for $b \in C$, $b \in y$ if and only if $b$ lies in $\mathfrak{m}_W$; and $W$ is the localisation of $B$ at the prime $\{b \in B : b \in \mathfrak{m}_W\}$, in the sense that $f \in W$ exactly when $f = g/h$ with $g,h \in B$, $h \notin \mathfrak{m}_W$. The hypothesis `hEQ` has five clauses (summarised here): for every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field of $A$ there is a surjection $\rho$ from $B$ onto the Drinfeld coordinate ring [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q (ResidueField A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) whose kernel is $\{b : b \in \mathfrak{m}_W\}$, which is compatible with $A \to \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ and which, for each level automorphism $\tau$ attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W$, intertwines $\tau$ with the action of an element $(\overline{\gamma},c)$ of [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) through `hAction`, with $c \ne 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \ne \mathrm{id}$; $B$ is stable under all level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma_0(M')$; every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$ is the image of $\mathfrak{m}_W \cap B$ under some level automorphism attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$; an element of $B$ carried into $\mathfrak{m}_W$ by all such automorphisms is divisible by $\varpi$; and a level automorphism attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $y$ preserves $W$.
--
--   An end is given by a subring $O$ of $K$ with `hO`: there exist $a \in J$ with $a \ne 0$ in $K$ and a maximal ideal $P$ of the chart $B_a$ generated over $C$ by $\{x \in K : xa \in J\}$, such that $O$ is the localisation of $B_a$ at $P$ inside $K$, every element of $y$ which lies in $O$ is a non-unit of $O$, and $B \not\subseteq O$. In addition `hOW`: $O \subseteq W$; `hOloc`: $O$ is local; `hOnoe`: $O$ is Noetherian; `hCO`: $C \subseteq O$. The last hypothesis `hIgStab` asserts that every valuation subring $V$ of $K$ such that the elements of $L$ lying in $V$ are exactly those coming from $A$, $\varpi$ lies in $\mathfrak{m}_V$, $C \subseteq V$, and some $c \in C$ has $p(c)$ a unit of $V$ for every monic polynomial $p$ over $A$, is stable under every level automorphism attached to some $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$.
--
--   Under these hypotheses there exist an integer $n \ge 1$ and an element $s \in C$ with $s \in J^n$ and $s \ne 0$ in $K$ such that:
--
--   (i) $s$ divides a power of $\varpi$ in $C$: there are $k \in \mathbb{N}$ and an element of $C$ whose product with $s$ is $\varpi^k$;
--
--   (ii) $\tau(s) = s$ for every $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and every $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ which is a level automorphism attached to $\gamma^{-1}$;
--
--   (iii) $\varpi_t^{\,n}s^{-1} \in W$;
--
--   (iv) for every valuation subring $V$ of $K$ such that the elements of $L$ lying in $V$ are exactly those coming from $A$, and such that $\varpi$, whenever it lies in $V$, lies in $\mathfrak{m}_V$: if $j \in V$, if $p(j)$ is a unit of $V$ for every monic polynomial $p$ over $A$ (whenever $p(j) \in V$), and if $O \subseteq V$, then $s$, whenever it lies in $V$, is a unit of $V$;
--
--   (v) for every valuation subring $V$ of $K$ satisfying the same two conditions on $L$ and $\varpi$: if $j \in V$, if $p(j)$ is a unit of $V$ for every monic polynomial $p$ over $A$ (whenever $p(j) \in V$), and if some element of $O$ fails to lie in $V$, then there exists $c \in J^n$ with $c\,s^{-1} \notin V$.
--
--   This belongs to the analysis of the special fibre at $q$ of the integral model of the modular curve of level $(q\ell)^2M'$: it produces, near a blown-up supersingular point, a $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$-invariant element of the $n$-th power of the centre $J$ which divides a power of the uniformiser, has the prescribed order on the exceptional valuation $W$, is a unit along every Igusa-type valuation dominating the given end $O$, and is non-minimal along those that do not. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_verticalUnit_pow_centre_of_end_blowupChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_verticalUnit_pow_centre_of_end_blowupChart), and is proved from `exists_labelUnit_chartAlgFin_of_end_blowupChart`, `exists_pow_mem_centre_pow_of_labelUnit_of_end_blowupChart` and `exists_mem_centre_not_mem_maximalIdeal_of_igusaType_blowupChart`.
